From 1 and 3, we can infer ¬(Wn ∨ Wm) (Neither Nancy nor Marvin are at work).
From 2, we can infer ~Wm (Marvin is not at work) because he is a lawyer and out to dinner.
From 1 and 3, we can infer Wm (Marvin is at work) because he is not at work.
Now, we can infer that the premises are inconsistent. Therefore, we can conclude that not everything is not at work, i.e. everything is at work.

The correct answer is: A. Either Nancy or Marvin are at work. All lawyers are not at work if they are out to dinner. Nancy is a lawyer and out to dinner. So not everything is at work.
